==Battleground==
*1 [[Assassin Bear]] spawns after 233.33 seconds<sup>7,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Ms. Sign]] spawns as the boss after 233.33 seconds<sup>7,000f</sup>.
*1 [[St. Dober]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[M. Ost]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Elder Sloth]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The point of this stage is to beat the 3 bosses before the assassin bear destroys you, so you need to quickly kill everything. Alternatively, you could feasibly cheese by pinning the Sloth to the base through crowd control and using Long Distance units to snipe the base, or clipping a fast cat through, such as [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train]] or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]].

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]]: With his spammability and DPS against Aliens, he'll effortlessly destroy Elder Sloth, even on {{3c}}.
*[[Eggy Cat (Rare Cat)|Easter Egg Cat]]/[[Ancient Egg: N110 (Rare Cat)|Farmboy Cat]]: Incredibly potent anti-Angel crowd-controllers that work even better than [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]]. Their Single Attack is not a hindrance here because of the enemy limit of 1.
*[[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet the Maiko]]: A stack of Juliets can freeze St. Dober in place easily. Her long foreswing means she might not work as the only crowd-controller though.
*[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]/[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]]: Great anti-Angel attackers for St. Dober. Cafeteria Cat is the better overall choice here, but is harder to get.
*[[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]: Always a great attacker for M. Ost.
*[[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Future Cat]]/[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize Cat]]: Good meatshields against M. Ost, goes great with Slapsticks' Weaken Talent.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]]: If you have him, he can make the M. Ost way easier to deal with.
*[[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer]]: If you have this uncommon collaboration cat then it may be worth it to use him alongside Freeze Up [[Cat Combo]]s and make 2/3 of the bosses far easier to get rid of, altough he may need assistance from the [[Ototo Corps|Thunderbolt Cannon]] to properly permafreeze Saint Dober
*[[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Soractes]]: While not available on the first play of this stage, Soractes trivializes the end of the stage on 2-4♛. He serves as a good (albeit inconsistent) freeze versus St. Dober as well as trivializing the time gimmick of the stage through conjure so long as it's not used before Assassin Bear comes out.

==Trivia==
*Hall of the Four Kings may be a reference to the [[wikipedia:Hall of Four Heavenly Kings|Hall of Four Heavenly Kings]], a hall inside a shanmen (mount gate) in Chinese Buddhist temples that contains statues of the [[wikipedia:Four Heavenly Kings|Four Heavenly Kings]], a quartet of Buddhist gods who each rule over a cardinal direction of the world. The term "Four Heavenly Kings" has been used throughout Japanese pop culture to refer to other powerful groups of four, such as a [[wikia:toriko:Four Heavenly Kings|quartet of Gourmet Hunters]] in ''[[wikipedia:Toriko|Toriko]]'' and the four highest-ranking members of [[wikia:streetfighter:Shadaloo|Shadaloo]] in ''[[Street Fighter Collaboration Event|Street Fighter]]''.

